+Disabling retries
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Pass ``enabled=False`` to call the function exactly once, without retry
+callbacks, waits, or exception wrapping. Exceptions propagate unchanged.
+Retries are enabled by default. This option is also available on ``Retrying``
+and ``AsyncRetrying``.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @retry(enabled=False)
+    def development_call():
+        raise RuntimeError("propagates directly")
+
+You can also disable retries for an existing decorated function with
+``development_call.retry_with(enabled=False)()``.
+
 Changing Arguments at Run Time
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
